<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27403" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lysĭas</span></b> , ae,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λυσίας</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Son of Cephalus, a famous orator of Athens</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tum fuit Lysias, quem jam prope audeas oratorem
					perfectum dicere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 9, 35</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 85, 293</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de
				Or. 1, 54, 231</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Or. 9, 29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 10,
				1, 78</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12,
				10, 24</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lysĭăcus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to the orator Lysias</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gracilitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 12, 10, 24</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A physician</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 5,
			18</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A celebrated sculptor</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 36, 5,
				4, § 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
